{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Is it well?</b> Do you have well-being in bodily health? For health indeed obtains when the opposites are in equilibrium — when none of the opposites predominates over its contrary." "<b>The old father of whom you spoke, etc.</b> For the well-being of an old man declines rapidly, as our Sages of blessed memory said: the lips of the elderly grow slack and their ears grow heavy."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:25.839873494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}